{
  "id": 206522840,
  "iid": 9830,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "RTPS: Dynamically grow array of elements",
  "description": "It is difficult to check if the putative number of elements\n(retrieved as a 32 bit unsigned integer) is correct, since the\nnumber of bytes consumed by each element varies. If the number\nof elements is bogusly large, this can lead to a huge amount\nof unused allocated memory when there is a BoundsError.\n\nRather than immediately allocating memory for the array of info\nelements, use a wmem_array_t with a reasonable maximum initial\nsize and grow it as necessary as we process elements.\n\nAdd a wmem_array_finalize function, similar to wmem_strbuf_finalize,\nthat truncates and returns the underlying array and frees the\nwmem_array_t structure.\n\nFix #18854",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2023-02-19T14:38:19.262Z",
  "updated_at": "2023-03-17T23:45:45.040Z",
